Article 7 (Applicability to examination of eligibility for largest shareholder)
`Article 32 shall begin to apply where a person fails to meet requirements for maintaining qualification due to an event that occurs after this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Transitional Measures Following Changes in Qualifications for Executive Officers)
Notwithstanding Articles 5, 6, and 19(10), former provisions of the Banking Act, the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act, the Insurance Business Act, the Mutual Savings Banks Act, the Specialized Credit Finance Business Act, and the Financial Holding Companies Act shall apply to qualifications for executive officers who work for a financial company as at the time this Act enters into force, until the end of their respective terms of office.
Article 9 (Transitional measure concerning restrictions on concurrent office)
Notwithstanding Articles 6 and 10, a person who holds concurrent office as an executive officer or employee of another company, while serving as an executive officer of a financial company, as at the time this Act enters into force, shall be deemed to hold concurrent office under this Act until the end of his or her term of office as an executive officer of a financial company or until the end of his or her term of office as an executive officer of another company, whichever comes earlier (if the term of office expires not less than three years after this Act enters into force or if an executive officer holds concurrent office as an employee of another company, the term of office shall be deemed to expire on the third anniversary of the enforcement date of this Act).
Article 10 (Transitional measures concerning appointment, dismissal of major operating officers)
Notwithstanding Article 8, a major operating officer who serves or works for a financial company as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a major operating officer appointed under this Act until the end of his or her term of office (if the term of office expires not less than three years after this Act enters into force or if an executive officer holds concurrent office as an employee of another company, the term of office shall be deemed to expire on the third anniversary of the enforcement date of this Act).
Article 11 (Transitional measures concerning composition and operation of board of directors)
Every financial company (excluding financial companies that fall under Article 3(3)) shall form a board of directors in accordance with Article 12 until the date of the first general meeting of shareholders held after this Act enters into force.
Article 12 (Transitional measures concerning establishment of committees within the board of directors)
A financial company (excluding a financial company under Article 3(3)) shall establish a committee for recommendation of candidates for executive officers, an audit committee, a risk management committee, and a remuneration committee pursuant to Article 16 by the date of the first general meeting of shareholders convened after this Act enters into force.
Article 13 (Transitional measures concerning appointment of audit committee members and full-time auditors)
(1) A financial company (excluding a financial company under Article 3(3)) shall appoint Audit Committee members in compliance with Article 19(1) through (7) and (10) by the date of the first general meeting of shareholders convened after this Act enters into force.
(2) A financial company prescribed by Presidential Decree pursuant to the main clause of Article 19(8) shall appoint a full-time auditor in compliance with Article 19(8) through (10) by the date of the first general meeting of shareholders convened after this Act enters into force.
Article 14 (Transitional measures concerning compliance officers)
(1) A compliance officer of a financial company holding office as at the time this Act enters into force expires shall be deemed a compliance officer appointed under this Act until his or her term of office expires (if the term of office expires two years after the date this Act enters into force, or where he or she is in office as an employee, it shall be the date on which a second year falls since the Act enters into force).
(2) Notwithstanding Article 26, the qualification requirements for compliance officers in paragraph (1) shall be governed by the previous Banking Act, the Capital Market and Financial Investment Services Act, the Insurance Business Act, the Mutual Savings Bank Act, the Credit Specialized Financial Business Act, and the Financial Holding Companies Act.
Article 15 (Transitional measures concerning sanctions)
The violations of the previous Banking Act, the Capital Market and Financial Investment Services Act, the Insurance Business Act, the Mutual Savings Bank Act, the Credit Specialized Financial Business Act, and the Financial Holding Companies before this Act enters into force Act shall be governed by the previous provisions.
Article 16 (Transitional measure concerning administrative fines)
The violations of the previous Banking Act, the Capital Market and Financial Investment Services Act, the Insurance Business Act, the Mutual Savings Bank Act, the Credit Specialized Financial Business Act, and the Financial Holding Companies before this Act enters into force Act shall be governed by the previous provisions.
Article 17 (Transitional measures concerning incompetent persons)
A person who has already been declared incompetent or limited incompetent as at the time of enforcement of this Act shall be deemed a person under adult guardianship or limited guardianship under this Act until the judgment is revoked or loses effect.
Article 18 Omitted.

